      "key": "I300_GEOMETRY_READING",
      "kind": "observation",
      "value": "At 300 iterations the hinge DOES move the cosine (0.999965 -> 0.872725; fraction of pairs at cos >= 0.9 falls 1.000 -> 0.530) while making the participation-ratio effective dimension WORSE (1.93 -> 1.28 of d=128) and raising per-dimension sd 48x (0.00057 -> 0.02727). Those move together only if the hinge-on gestalts spread along essentially ONE axis with sign variation -- an antipodal 1-D structure, not a restored space. Cosine improves because antipodal pairs have low cosine; the space is not less degenerate, it is degenerate differently. This is why the verdict rests on the effective dimension and the memory ablation, not on the cosine alone.",
      "how": "I300_HINGEON/HINGEOFF allpairs_cos_mean, frac_pairs_cos_ge_0.9, effective_dim, per_dim_sd rows"
    }
