  "verdict": {
    "falsifier": "The gestalt collapse is caused by the missing srep_norm_penalty. Restore the reference's hinge with srep_norm_reg_weight, retrain identically, and the gestalt space stays non-degenerate.",
    "outcome": "falsified",
    "detail": "FALSIFIED, with one honest qualification the brief's framing did not anticipate. The hinge binds decisively: the training penalty falls 179.19 -> 0.031 at 100 iterations (5798x) and 21.77 -> 0.0004 at 300, and the pre-normalisation srep norm falls 14.67 -> 0.80 (100 it) / 21.77 -> 0.82 (300 it), from 15-20x outside the reference's [0.9, 1.1] band to just below it. The collapse survives anyway. (1) 100 iterations, 3 seeds: all-pairs gestalt cosine 0.99975 +- 0.00020 (off) vs 0.99586 +- 0.00195 (on); 100% of all 73536 sentence pairs at cos >= 0.9 in BOTH arms; effective dimension 1.96 +- 1.52 vs 2.77 +- 1.04 of d = 128, overlapping sds. Indistinguishable. (2) 300 iterations, 2 seeds: the arms DO separate on cosine (0.999965 +- 0.000018 vs 0.872725 +- 0.005473; fraction at cos >= 0.9 1.000 vs 0.530 +- 0.010), but the effective dimension gets WORSE (1.93 +- 1.10 vs 1.28 +- 0.04) while per-dimension sd rises 48x -- i.e. the hinge-on gestalts spread along one antipodal axis rather than recovering a space. 1.28 of 128 dimensions is not a non-degenerate gestalt space, so the claim as stated dies. (3) The decisive limb is the memory, and it is inert in both arms at both iteration counts. Deleting the entire 16-slot memory changes the masked real-token NLL by +0.033% +- 0.003% (hinge off) and -0.044% +- 0.060% (hinge on) at 300 iterations -- both indistinguishable from zero, and no better than cycle 11's 0.29%. Cross-attention KL from uniform stays 0.0099 - 0.054 nats against ln 16 = 2.7726. (4) The LM loss is NOT the tradeoff: the hinge arm is equal or slightly better (final train CE 0.1008 +- 0.0006 vs 0.1059 +- 0.0055 at 300 iterations; masked real-token NLL 1.534 +- 0.034 vs 1.548 +- 0.017). The hinge is free, and it should be restored on correctness grounds -- it just does not buy a usable memory. (5) Control anchor: the hinge-off arm reproduces cycle 11 bit-exactly -- its seed-0 loss trajectory at every 25 iterations is 4.96007, 0.51682, 0.25028, 0.19731, 0.17076, 0.14948, 0.13975, 0.13080, 0.12231, 0.11072, 0.10482, 0.10291, 0.10207, digit-for-digit cycle 11's published row, and 3-seed step-0 CE is 4.977344 +- 0.017788 vs its 4.977347 +- 0.017786. (6) Instrument check: the untrained model on the same measurement code gives cosine 0.487, 1.1% of pairs at cos >= 0.9 and 16.75 effective dimensions, so the instrument resolves a healthy space. Seed counts are 3 (100 it) and 2 (300 it); an sd over two or three samples is weak and the arm gaps that matter here are orders of magnitude, not sd-scale."
  },
